<title>BULGARIA: Yield rises to 0.43 pct on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises to 0.43 pct on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yield rose to 0.43 percent on Bulgaria's Finance Ministry four-week discount T-bills at the daily auction on Thursday, central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The average yield to maturity at Wednesday's auction was 0.40 percent, down from 0.42 percent on Tuesday and 0.47 percent on Monday.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with a par value of 10 billion levs and no minimum acceptable price set in advance.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3040397005</p>
<p> Maturity			four weeks</p>
<p> Par value		     10,000 million levs</p>
<p> Issue date		    June 27</p>
<p> Maturity date		 July 25</p>
<p> Bids received		 10,051.5 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   99.57 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 10,000 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  99.57 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     0.43 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
</text>
